│ To resolve the issue where rendering empty_form crashes when       │
│ empty_permitted is passed to form_kwargs, we need to modify the    │
│ empty_form method in the BaseFormSet class. The goal is to ensure  │
│ that empty_permitted is ignored when rendering the empty_form, as  │
│ it is irrelevant for this specific case.                           │
│                                                                    │
│ The relevant code is located in the empty_form method, where       │
│ empty_permitted is currently being set to True unconditionally. We │
│ will modify this to ensure that it does not depend on the          │
│ form_kwargs passed to the formset.                                 │
│                                                                    │
│ Here’s the patch:                                                  │
│                                                                    │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
│ ┃                         modification 1                         ┃ │
│ ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛ │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  [file]django/forms/formsets.py[/file]                             │
│  [original]                                                        │
│          form = self.form(                                         │
│              auto_id=self.auto_id,                                 │
│              prefix=self.add_prefix("__prefix__"),                 │
│              empty_permitted=True,                                 │
│              use_required_attribute=False,                         │
│              **self.get_form_kwargs(None),                         │
│              renderer=self.renderer,                               │
│          )                                                         │
│  [/original]                                                       │
│  [patched]                                                         │
│          form_kwargs = self.get_form_kwargs(None)                  │
│          form_kwargs.pop('empty_permitted', None)  # Ignore        │
│  empty_permitted for empty_form                                    │
│          form = self.form(                                         │
│              auto_id=self.auto_id,                                 │
│              prefix=self.add_prefix("__prefix__"),                 │
│              use_required_attribute=False,                         │
│              **form_kwargs,                                        │
│              renderer=self.renderer,                               │
│          )                                                         │
│  [/patched]                                                        │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ This modification ensures that the empty_permitted key is removed  │
│ from the form_kwargs dictionary before it is passed to the form    │
│ constructor, thus preventing any KeyError related to               │
│ empty_permitted when rendering the empty_form. This change is      │
│ minimal and preserves the existing functionality of the formset    │
│ while addressing the issue directly.                               │
